# GitHub and Git remotes

## Scope

Applies when reading GitHub repos, using `gh`/GitHub MCP, or performing any git remote write (push, PR, issue, release, etc.).

## Reading repositories

When given GitHub links, try **GitHub MCP** first, then **SSH**, then **HTTP/S**.

Prefer GitHub MCP for API operations (issues, PRs, releases, metadata) when available.

## Creating repositories

Create a repo **only when the user specifically asks** (`gh`, GitHub MCP, or web UI). Defaults unless overridden:

- **Owner:** OWilliamson
- **Default branch:** `main`
- **Visibility:** private

## Commits and pull requests

- Use **complete sentences**; put the **why** in the body when not obvious from the title.
- **Scope detail** to the change — short for small fixes; enough context for larger or risky changes.
- Use **full paths or URLs** for file and web references.

## Repository classes

Treat the GitHub user/org in a remote URL or API path as **OWilliamson** when it matches this account **case-insensitively**.

| Class | Writable? |
|-------|-----------|
| **OWilliamson fork** — fork under the OWilliamson account | Yes (visibility rules below) |
| **OWilliamson private repo** — under OWilliamson, not public | Yes |
| **Company or org repo** — any org namespace, even with collaborator access | Read-only |
| **Collaborator repo** — another user's namespace, not OWilliamson | Read-only |
| **Upstream of your fork** — parent of an OWilliamson fork | Read-only |
| **Everything else** not listed above as writable | Read-only |

Do **not** create forks. If asked, explain this profile does not allow fork creation.

## Write policy by visibility

- **OWilliamson private repos and OWilliamson forks (private):** read/write — push, pull, branch, routine GitHub updates without asking each time.
- **Public repos** (any namespace): write actions **only when the user specifically asks** for that action.

## Before any push or remote write

Verify the **target remote URL** (or API repo path) matches the intended repository class. Do not push to `origin` by habit.

## Read-only repositories

On read-only classes, do **not** `git push` (including force-push); open or update PRs, issues, comments, releases, or wiki pages; or run GitHub MCP / `gh` commands that create, update, delete, or publish.

**Allowed:** inspect via MCP or web, search, `git clone`, `git fetch`, `git pull` for study or local builds. Local-only Git with no remote write is fine.

If the user asks to write to a read-only repo, explain this profile treats it as read-only.

## Restricted operations (all repos)

Unless the user **specifically asks** for that exact action:

- **Destructive:** do not delete repos, transfer ownership, rename default branch, or change visibility.
- **Deny without exception:** fork creation; GitHub Actions (workflows, secrets, variables, runners, dispatch); Packages/GHCR publish or settings; Discussions; Projects (classic and v2); branch protection changes.

## Excuse → reality

| Excuse | Reality |
|--------|---------|
| "`origin` is probably mine." | Verify remote URL against repository class before every push. |
| "Public OWilliamson repo — I can push." | Public repos need an explicit write request per action. |
| "Org repo but I have admin." | Org namespaces are read-only in this profile. |
| "I'll fork to contribute." | Fork creation is denied; explain and stop. |
